00:21:53,686 --> 00:21:55,699
I'm sorry, Johnny.
you know I like my boys young.

482
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:57,200
And you just aren't so anymore.

483
00:21:57,847 --> 00:21:59,100
Oh, let them go, honey.

484
00:22:01,517 --> 00:22:03,600
You're in for the best afternoon

485
00:22:04,383 --> 00:22:05,549
of your life!

486
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,721
We have almost the same blood.

487
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:14,200
How did my life go so wrong?

488
00:22:15,134 --> 00:22:17,200
Genetic mutations can be so cruel.

489
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,403
- This is Sam.
- Hey Sam.

490
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,084
- When you get a second, can we talk?
- Sure.

491
00:22:27,281 --> 00:22:28,516
Thanks.

492
00:22:29,784 --> 00:22:31,276
I think I'm in trouble.

493
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:33,546
I'll be right back.

494
00:22:33,649 --> 00:22:35,363
So. How was the day, boys?

495
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:37,899
Well, Drama's got
the cleanest asshole in America

496
00:22:38,053 --> 00:22:40,333
and I learned that
passion begins after 40.

497
00:22:40,571 --> 00:22:42,989
- So I'd say it was a pretty good day.
- It sounds like it.

498
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,500
Yo, what's up?

499
00:22:46,236 --> 00:22:47,496
Can you guys give us a minute?

500
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,074
- It's my house, E.
- Johnny.

501
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:51,879
Yeah, sure, bro.

502
00:22:52,011 --> 00:22:54,565
Yeah, who knows? Maybe I'll even
take a girl from you this time.

503
00:22:54,599 --> 00:22:56,777
- because I am on a hot streak.
- Shut up.

504
00:22:57,086 --> 00:22:59,682
Yeah, this ain't a house.
It's a condo and it ain't a big one.

505
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:02,250
So you're mad at me?

506
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:04,662
- You called me pizza boy.
- No, I didn't.

507
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,983
Yeah, you did.
You called me pizza boy just like Ari.

508
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,167
I was pissed.
I was down 100 grand on a soccer game.

509
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,543
- What?
- Yeah, don't worry. I got it all back.

510
00:23:12,893 --> 00:23:15,972
- And I won $100,000 on Brazil.
- Are you fucking kidding me?

511
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:17,134
No,

512
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,513
Come on.
You wanna hit the palm for lobbies?

513
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,700
Come on, it's a good day.

514
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:25,100
- No it's not. I'm pissed.
- I'm sorry.

515
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:27,099
You know what?
Don't give me that shit.

516
00:23:27,100 --> 00:23:29,699
You know, you tell me
I'm not a filmmaker, and that's fine.

517
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,608
But you know what?
I found the script.

518
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:34,014
You didn't and Ari didn't.
I picked the director.

519
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:36,427
And I got somebody to buy this movie

520
00:23:36,487 --> 00:23:38,400
and bail us out
of our financial problems.

521
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:40,800
- What do you mean?
- I brought it to Harvey.

522
00:23:41,376 --> 00:23:44,200
He wants it, Vince.
I got him to make us an offer.

523
00:23:44,553 --> 00:23:47,013
$25 million.
It takes final cut away from Billy.

524
00:23:47,150 --> 00:23:49,528
It's what's best for us
and it's what's best for the movie.

525
00:23:49,613 --> 00:23:50,848
- You got an offer?
- Yeah.

526
00:23:50,933 --> 00:23:52,288
And if we get rejected from Cannes

527
00:23:52,339 --> 00:23:54,874
and that goes public we may
never get an offer like that again.

528
00:23:54,908 --> 00:23:56,258
You got an offer off a trailer?

529
00:23:58,988 --> 00:24:00,496
That is amazing.

530
00:24:00,896 --> 00:24:02,600
Yeah, I can spin some dough, huh?

531
00:24:02,850 --> 00:24:03,900
Look, E,

532
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:06,096
I know you're doing
what you think is best,

533
00:24:06,199 --> 00:24:07,859
and I was wrong
about what I said today.

534
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:10,806
And I do appreciate how much
you really have done. I really do.

535
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,200
But is it possible you're wrong too?

536
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:14,859
- How?
- About the movie.

537
00:24:15,009 --> 00:24:17,271
Maybe you really are too close.
Is that possible?

538
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:21,300
Maybe, but I'd like to be protected
in case we don't get into Cannes.

539
00:24:21,620 --> 00:24:22,889
We did get into Cannes.

540
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,347
What?

541
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:27,056
The movie got into Cannes.
I just talked to Walsh an hour ago.

542
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:29,921
- I don't believe it.
- Well, believe it, because you made...

543
00:24:30,024 --> 00:24:31,756
We made a great film.

544
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:34,489
A film I don't think we should
sell until we get to the festival.

545
00:24:34,557 --> 00:24:35,663
We got into Cannes?

546
00:24:36,030 --> 00:24:37,400
Maybe you should watch it again.

547
00:24:37,733 --> 00:24:38,800
Maybe.

